WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:08.889
Aqua Regia, Royal Water, is a mixture of two
acids,

00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:12.910
hydrochloric acid and nitric acid. The reason
it’s called

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.019
‘royal water’ is because it dissolves
gold. Gold has

00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:21.080
fascinated people for thousands of years because
it

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.500
doesn’t dissolve in anything, doesn’t
tarnish, always

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.029
looks nice and shiny, and this was a material
that could

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:34.370
dissolve it. So it was really something, the
lion of the

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.190
acids, like the lion of an animal, king of
the animals!

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:44.990
So Aqua Regia is a mixture of hydrochloric
acid and

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:50.059
nitric acid, but each of those is a mixture
of something

00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:53.530
in water, a solution of something in water.
So

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:58.060
hydrochloric acid is hydrogen chloride, which
is an atom

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:02.520
of chlorine bonded to an atom of hydrogen,
now the

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.250
importance of this is that when the HCl dissolves
in

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.389
water the bond between them breaks and you
get

00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:16.340
chloride ions, Cl-, and H+, hydrogen ions,
and it is the

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.259
formation of hydrogen ions which makes something
an

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:22.399
acid. So when you have the mixture of all
these ions you

00:01:22.399 --> 00:01:25.659
get quite a soup. Now the exciting thing about
Aqua

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:31.319
Regia is that neither of the two acids by
themselves can

00:01:31.319 --> 00:01:36.749
dissolve gold. Nitric acid doesn’t really
react with gold

00:01:36.749 --> 00:01:43.390
very much at all, and HCl, hydrogen chloric
acid can’t

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.979
get a hold of the gold to get the reaction
going. But if

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:52.029
you can gold into solution then it can react.
So what

00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:59.639
happens is as follows: the nitric acid can
attack the gold

00:01:59.639 --> 00:02:04.289
and a very small proportion of the gold, relatively
few

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:09.361
atoms, are persuaded into going into solution
and there

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:11.911
is an equilibrium, some are coming off and
an equal

00:02:11.911 --> 00:02:16.329
number are going back on to the surface. So
if you just

00:02:16.329 --> 00:02:20.120
have the gold in there it appears to be unaffected.
If you

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.410
were on an atomic scale you would see atoms
coming

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:27.110
off and others going back, but nothing changes.
But

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:31.650
when you have the hydrogen chloride there,
the chloride

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.140
ions can attack the gold and turn them into
a different

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:38.930
compound so they can’t go back. So more
and more and

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:43.950
more gold atoms come off, until eventually
all of it is

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:50.109
converted to another acid, which is an acid
of gold with

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:55.340
four chlorine atoms around it. This material
is then quite

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.709
soluble in water, so provided you don’t
have too much

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:03.730
gold it will all dissolve. And once you have
the solution,

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.859
you will get a brownish solution or greenish
solution

00:03:06.859 --> 00:03:09.720
depending how much gold is in there.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:16.530
I’ve never seen Aqua Regia because it’s
quite a nasty

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:22.290
material, you have to use it in the fume cupboard,
because otherwise, because of these fumes

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:27.079
of NO2 and
unless you want to dissolve gold, you don’t

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:31.540
usually need
this. It is a pretty good cleaning material

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.620
if you have
glassware, beakers things like that that you

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:40.120
can’t clean
any other way. The sort of last resort is

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:44.629
‘we’ll try Aqua
Regia to see if that’ll do it?’ you know

00:03:44.629 --> 00:03:48.939
really bang the
dirt. And it sometimes works, not always,

00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:50.760
depends what
the dirt is.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:56.099
Aqua Regia is Latin, for Aqua is the Latin
for ‘water’ as

00:03:56.099 --> 00:04:01.510
in ‘aqueduct’ and also we use it in English
and the word

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:07.019
‘aqueous’ and things like that. There
is…and Regia is the

00:04:07.019 --> 00:04:12.650
Latin for ‘royal’ as in ‘regal’, and
comes from the word

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.799
Rex which means the word ‘king’ in Latin.

00:04:15.799 --> 00:04:19.539
Well there is quite a famous story about Aqua
Regia and

00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:24.569
the institute of Niels Bohr, the Nobel Prize
winner, who

00:04:24.569 --> 00:04:28.450
had an institute in Copenhagen and at the
beginning of

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.990
the Second World War when Denmark was still
neutral,

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:37.390
two German Nobel Prize winners, Max von Laue
and

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.440
Frank who had won the Nobel Prize before the
Second

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.060
World War sent their gold medals for safe-keeping
to

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:54.139
Denmark and someone in the lab at, in Denmark,
dissolved them in Aqua Regia and just put

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:56.759
the bottle on
the shelf where there were lots of other bottles

00:04:56.759 --> 00:04:59.990
of
chemicals and they stayed there the whole

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:03.379
war because
nobody realised that they were gold and after

00:05:03.379 --> 00:05:08.120
the war
the gold was recovered, the medals were re-struck

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.259
and
given back to the Nobel Prize winners.

